<resources>
    <!--
        The launcher icon's background follows the wallpaper. The glyph does
        not: it stays white, which is what the icon has always looked like and
        what keeps it recognisable whatever the palette does.

        accent1_400 is a light tone of the wallpaper palette, and it is the
        lightest one white strokes still sit on. Going up to 300 or 200 starts
        losing the glyph on a pale wallpaper, so this is the light end rather
        than the middle.

        An absolute tone, not a theme colour, so the icon looks the same
        whether the phone is in light or dark mode, which is right for
        something that lives on the home screen.

        No values-v31 copy: minSdk is 31, so there is no device here without
        these resources, and a second file would only be a second place to
        forget.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">@android:color/system_accent1_400</color>
    <color name="ic_launcher_foreground">#FFFFFF</color>
</resources>
